      <title>Verizon Beats, Brazil in Focus | Stock Movers</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-10-26/verizon-beats-brazil-in-focus-stock-movers-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">a8f8b0d9a60ff923cec3bea9</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:29:10 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Today's biggest winners and losers in the stock market.

On this episode of Stock Movers:

- Verizon (VZ) shares are moving after it reported its strongest third-quarter performance in wireless customer additions in five years, adding a net 406,000 monthly phone lines.

- PagSeguro (PAGS) is among the many Brazil-linked stocks sliding this morning after President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva won Brazil’s runoff election with 51.8% of the vote, defeating Flávio Bolsonaro who received 48.2%.

- Surgery Partners (SGRY) is moving on news Bon Secours Mercy Health is in late-stage talks to buy a majority stake in Surgery Partners, the Financial Times reported. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
